From: Bellatrix contributors
Subject: [PATCH] AROSTCP: start stack before network managers

WirelessManager links against bsdsocket.library. Starting it before AROSTCP
means its OpenLibrary("bsdsocket.library") fails and its MUI AppIcon never
survives long enough to appear. Bring the stack up first, then start the
wireless and mobile managers that consume it.

---
 workbench/network/stacks/AROSTCP/S/Package-Startup | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/workbench/network/stacks/AROSTCP/S/Package-Startup b/workbench/network/stacks/AROSTCP/S/Package-Startup
index 20f0205790..9f0221bf5e 100644
--- a/workbench/network/stacks/AROSTCP/S/Package-Startup
+++ b/workbench/network/stacks/AROSTCP/S/Package-Startup
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@ Protect S/stopnet s add quiet
 
 if ${AROSTCP/AutoRun} eq "True"
 
+  C:Execute S/startnet
+
   if ${AROSTCP/WirelessAutoRun} eq "True"
     Run >NIL: QUIET C:WirelessManager ${AROSTCP/WirelessDevice}
   EndIf
@@ -16,8 +18,6 @@ if ${AROSTCP/AutoRun} eq "True"
     Run >NIL: QUIET C:ModemManager
   EndIf
 
-  C:Execute S/startnet
-
   if EXISTS ENV:AROSTCP/ServerAutoMounts
     Mount ${AROSTCP/ServerAutoMounts} 
   EndIf
-- 
2.39.5
